Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Three everyday moments in China that aren't about being polite.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.84,0:00:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Names first.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.47,0:00:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,In the US, using your friend's mom's first name sounds friendly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.59,0:00:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,In many Chinese families, the name you choose maps the relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.44,0:00:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,"Auntie" places you; a first name skips a step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.12,0:00:20.28,Default,,0,0,0,,At the door, the same logic applies.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.53,0:00:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,In the US, tearing the paper off a gift is fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.10,0:00:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,In many Chinese homes, the thank-you comes first; the gift can wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.60,0:00:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not about the gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.06,0:00:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,It's about the person.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.62,0:00:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,At the table, it changes again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.77,0:00:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,In the US, a tip is part of the service.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.69,0:00:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,In China, the menu price is usually the whole price.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.19,0:00:43.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Extra can feel less like generosity — more like charity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.23,0:00:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Different rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.40,0:00:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Same instinct: respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.75,0:00:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Which one would you have gotten wrong?
